Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: rg35xx-sp: keep the RAM voltage the SPL set

The shared RG35XX device tree pins vdd-dram at 1.1V for LPDDR4, but the SP is
also sold with LPDDR3, which runs at 1.2V. The SPL finds out which one the
unit has and sets the voltage for it. With a range of 1.1V to 1.2V, Linux
leaves the regulator where it is, since it only moves a voltage outside the
range, so it neither undervolts LPDDR3 nor overvolts LPDDR4.
ROCKNIX instead sets 1.2V through its H700 ddr3 overlay, in its LPDDR3 build.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-sp.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-sp.dts
@@ -32,3 +32,12 @@
 		reg = <0x51>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * LPDDR4 runs at 1.1V and LPDDR3 at 1.2V. The SPL tries both and sets the
+ * voltage of the one that works; Linux keeps it, as it is inside this range.
+ */
+&reg_dcdc3 {
+	regulator-min-microvolt = <1100000>;
+	regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+};
